      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "By using the general term formula of the binomial expansion, the general term formula of $(x+y)^6$ is: $T_{r+1}=C_6^r\\cdot x^{6-r}\\cdot y^r$.\nLet $6-r=r$,\nWe get $2x^2y^4$,\nTherefore, the coefficient is $C_6^2=15$.\nSo, the answer is: $\\boxed{15}$.\nThe general term formula of $(x+y)^6$ is $T_{r+1}=C_6^r\\cdot x^{6-r}\\cdot y^r$. Let $6-r=r$, we get $2x^2y^4$, thus, the answer is $C_6^2=15$.\nThis question mainly tests the application of the general term formula and the expansion of binomials, which is quite basic.\n\nBased on the determination of the terrain types in locations ②, ④, and ⑤ in the figure, which of the following is true?\nA. Gentle forging, gentle to gentle, gentle and violent\nB. Gentle and violent, gentle to violent, violent\nC. Violent to gentler, gentle to gentler, gentler\nD. Violent to gentle, violent to gentle, gentler\nAnswer: C\n\nDuring the epidemic, a medical rescue center regularly disassembles and recomposes teams of white-coat doctors and nurses, just like assemble-to-team, attend-to-team, team-to-assembly, are-matched-up-to-specialization, are-specialization-to-assembly, or assemble-to-specialization... Various orderly pairing of the rescue team members. What 'seamless team pairing' embodies in the context of epidemic control is ____ ① Innovative and pioneering management methods, improving the characteristics of the rescue center community management ② Meeting the diverse social reality and demands of individual community members ③ Demarcating the corresponding responsibilities and rights of members of the medical rescue center ④ Closely integrating and relying on the public, strengthening the continuity of the rescue\nA. ①②\nB. ①③\nC. ②④\nD. ③④\nAnswer: C\n\nIf x^2 + ax - 3 can be factored into (x - 3)(x + b), then a + b equals ____ \nA. -1 \nB. 1 \nC. -2 \nD. 2\nAnswer: B\n\nThe primary factor influencing the distribution of Russia's passenger traffic volume is ____\nA. Climate\nB. Economy\nC. Technology\nD. Population distribution\nAnswer: B\n\nThe main factor causing the difference in climate between Regions A and B is ____\nA. Relative height\nB. Latitude\nC. Proximity to sea or land\nD. Plate tectonics\nAnswer: B\n\nWhich of the following statements, or both, correctly indicates that saltwater is a solution? ① Saltwater is a homogeneous and stable mixture; ② Saltwater is a clear, pale yellow liquid; ③ Saltwater is a pure substance; ④ Saltwater has a salty taste.\nA. ①③\nB. ②④\nC. ①②\nD. ①④\nAnswer: D\n\nOur country has had a provincial system since the Qin Dynasty (221 BC-207 BC). The provincial system had a long and glorious history in China, but just 120 years later, the provincial system was abolished. Which of the following options recaps this history correctly? ① The Qin Dynasty established the commandery-county system. ② The social elite was a typical example of a 'remote, harsh, and dangerous land.' ③ The capital was the center of national politics, economy, culture, military, and diplomacy. ④ The provincial official, a displaced management agent, was the highest administrative official appointed by the central government to oversee the local government.\nA. ①②③\nB. ①③④\nC. ①②④\nD. ①②③④\nAnswer: D",
