      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We use the binomial theorem, which states $(a+b)^n=\\binom{n}{0}a^nb^0+\\binom{n}{1}a^{n-1}b^1+\\cdots+\\binom{n}{n}a^0b^n=$ $\\binom{n}{0}a^nb^{n-1}+\\binom{n}{1}a^{n-1}b^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\binom{n}{n-1}ab^{n-1}+\\binom{n}{n}a^0b^n$, to compute the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term in the expansion of $(x+y)^6$.\n$\\binom{6}{4}x^{6-4}y^{6-4}=\\binom{6}{4}x^2y^4$ is the term with $x^2y^4$.\nSince $\\binom{6}{4}=15$, the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term in the expansion of $(x+y)^6$ is $\\boxed{15}$.",
